{"skill_id":"step-resp","version":2,"questions":[{"id":"step-resp-r1-q1","round":1,"type":"mc","prompt":"An LTI system has impulse response \\(h(t)\\). How is its unit-step response \\(s(t)\\) related to \\(h(t)\\)?","options":["\\(s(t)=\\dfrac{dh}{dt}\\)","\\(s(t)=h(t)\\) for every causal system","\\(s(t)=h(t-1)\\), a delayed copy of h","\\(s(t)=\\int_{0}^{t}h(\\tau)\\,d\\tau\\): the step response is the running integral of the impulse response"],"correct_index":3,"explanation":"A unit step is the running integral of an impulse, and an LTI system commutes with integration, so its output is the running integral of \\(h\\). Equivalently, \\(h(t)=ds/dt\\): the impulse response is the slope of the step response.\n• The derivative relation is backwards.\n• \\(s=h\\) would require the step and the impulse to be the same input.\n• A delay has nothing to do with it.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 390 100\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Block chain: a unit step u(t) enters an LTI block with impulse response h(t) and produces the step response s(t).\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" style=\"max-width:390px;width:100%;height:auto\"><rect x=\"20\" y=\"30\" width=\"90\" height=\"40\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"currentColor\" fill-opacity=\"0.10\"/><text x=\"65\" y=\"54\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">u(t)</text><line x1=\"110\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"50\"/><polygon points=\"130,50 123.6,52.7 123.6,47.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><rect x=\"130\" y=\"30\" width=\"90\" height=\"40\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"currentColor\" fill-opacity=\"0.10\"/><text x=\"175\" y=\"54\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">LTI: h(t)</text><line x1=\"220\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"240\" y2=\"50\"/><polygon points=\"240,50 233.6,52.7 233.6,47.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><rect x=\"240\" y=\"30\" width=\"90\" height=\"40\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"currentColor\" fill-opacity=\"0.10\"/><text x=\"285\" y=\"54\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">s(t)</text></svg>","figure_alt":"Block chain: a unit step u(t) enters an LTI block with impulse response h(t) and produces the step response s(t)."},{"id":"step-resp-r1-q2","round":1,"type":"numeric","prompt":"A first-order system obeys \\(\\tau\\,\\dfrac{dy}{dt}+y=Kx\\) with \\(K=2.5\\) and \\(\\tau=3\\ \\mathrm{s}\\). It starts at rest and a step of height 4 is applied to x at \\(t=0\\). What value does y settle to?","answer":10.0,"unit":"","tolerance":0.02,"explanation":"When everything stops changing, \\(dy/dt=0\\), so \\(y=Kx=2.5\\times4=10\\). The time constant only sets how fast y gets there, not where it ends.\n• Answering 4 ignores the gain K.\n• Answering 30 or 7.5 multiplies or divides by \\(\\tau\\), which does not affect the final value.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 210\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"First-order step response rising smoothly from 0 toward a flat final value, with no overshoot.\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" style=\"max-width:340px;width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"176\"/><polygon points=\"330,176 323.6,178.7 323.6,173.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"16\"/><polygon points=\"50,16 52.7,22.4 47.3,22.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"192\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">t (s)</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"12\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">y(t)</text><polyline points=\"50,176 52.2,170.6 54.5,165.5 56.8,160.6 59,155.8 61.2,151.3 63.5,147 65.8,142.8 68,138.8 70.2,134.9 72.5,131.3 74.8,128.1 77,124.3 79.2,121.1 81.5,118 83.8,115 86,112.1 88.2,109.4 90.5,106.7 92.8,104.2 95,101.8 97.2,99.4 99.5,97.4 101.8,95 104,93 106.2,91 108.5,89.1 110.8,87.3 113,85.6 115.2,83.9 117.5,82.3 119.8,80.8 122,79.3 124.2,77.9 126.5,76.5 128.8,75.2 131,74 133.2,72.8 135.5,71.6 137.8,70.5 140,69.5 142.2,68.5 144.5,67.5 146.8,66.6 149,65.8 151.2,64.8 153.5,64 155.8,63.2 158,62.5 160.2,61.7 162.5,61 164.8,60.4 167,59.7 169.2,59.1 171.5,58.5 173.8,58 176,57.4 178.2,56.9 180.5,56.4 182.8,55.9 185,55.5 187.2,55 189.5,54.6 191.8,54.2 194,53.8 196.2,53.4 198.5,53.1 200.8,52.7 203,52.4 205.2,52.1 207.5,51.8 209.8,51.5 212,51.2 214.2,51 216.5,50.7 218.8,50.5 221,50.2 223.2,50 225.5,49.8 227.8,49.6 230,49.4 232.2,49.2 234.5,49 236.8,48.8 239,48.6 241.2,48.5 243.5,48.3 245.8,48.2 248,48.1 250.2,47.9 252.5,47.8 254.8,47.6 257,47.5 259.2,47.4 261.5,47.3 263.8,47.2 266,47.1 268.2,47 270.5,46.9 272.8,46.8 275,46.7 277.2,46.6 279.5,46.6 281.8,46.5 284,46.4 286.2,46.3 288.5,46.3 290.8,46.2 293,46.1 295.2,46.1 297.5,46 299.8,46 302,45.9 304.2,45.9 306.5,45.8 308.8,45.8 311,45.7 313.2,45.7 315.5,45.6 317.8,45.6 320,45.6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></svg>","figure_alt":"First-order step response rising smoothly from 0 toward a flat final value, with no overshoot."},{"id":"step-resp-r1-q3","round":1,"type":"mc","prompt":"For the first-order step response \\(y(t)=y_\\infty\\left(1-e^{-t/\\tau}\\right)\\), what fraction of the final value \\(y_\\infty\\) has been reached at \\(t=\\tau\\)?","options":["About 63%","About 50%","About 37%","100%: the output arrives exactly at \\(t=\\tau\\)"],"correct_index":0,"explanation":"At \\(t=\\tau\\): \\(1-e^{-1}=0.632\\). After \\(2\\tau\\) it is 86%, after \\(3\\tau\\) 95%, and after \\(5\\tau\\) more than 99%; the exponential approaches its final value but never reaches it exactly.\n• 37% (\\(e^{-1}\\)) is the fraction still remaining at \\(t=\\tau\\), not the fraction reached.\n• 50% is reached earlier, at \\(t=\\tau\\ln2\\approx0.69\\tau\\).","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 210\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Normalized first-order step response; a dashed vertical line marks t = tau.\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" style=\"max-width:340px;width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"176\"/><polygon points=\"330,176 323.6,178.7 323.6,173.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"16\"/><polygon points=\"50,16 52.7,22.4 47.3,22.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"192\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">t (s)</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"12\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">y(t)</text><polyline points=\"50,176 52.2,170.6 54.5,165.5 56.8,160.6 59,155.8 61.2,151.3 63.5,147 65.8,142.8 68,138.8 70.2,134.9 72.5,131.3 74.8,128.1 77,124.3 79.2,121.1 81.5,118 83.8,115 86,112.1 88.2,109.4 90.5,106.7 92.8,104.2 95,101.8 97.2,99.4 99.5,97.4 101.8,95 104,93 106.2,91 108.5,89.1 110.8,87.3 113,85.6 115.2,84.1 117.5,82.3 119.8,80.8 122,79.3 124.2,77.9 126.5,76.5 128.8,75.4 131,74 133.2,72.8 135.5,71.6 137.8,70.5 140,69.5 142.2,68.5 144.5,67.5 146.8,66.6 149,65.8 151.2,64.8 153.5,64 155.8,63.2 158,62.5 160.2,61.7 162.5,61 164.8,60.4 167,59.7 169.2,59.1 171.5,58.5 173.8,58 176,57.4 178.2,56.9 180.5,56.4 182.8,55.9 185,55.5 187.2,55 189.5,54.6 191.8,54.2 194,53.8 196.2,53.4 198.5,53.1 200.8,52.7 203,52.4 205.2,52.1 207.5,51.8 209.8,51.5 212,51.2 214.2,51 216.5,50.7 218.8,50.5 221,50.2 223.2,50 225.5,49.8 227.8,49.6 230,49.4 232.2,49.2 234.5,49 236.8,48.8 239,48.6 241.2,48.5 243.5,48.3 245.8,48.2 248,48.1 250.2,47.9 252.5,47.8 254.8,47.6 257,47.5 259.2,47.4 261.5,47.3 263.8,47.2 266,47.1 268.2,47 270.5,46.9 272.8,46.8 275,46.7 277.2,46.6 279.5,46.6 281.8,46.5 284,46.4 286.2,46.3 288.5,46.3 290.8,46.2 293,46.1 295.2,46.1 297.5,46 299.8,46 302,45.9 304.2,45.9 306.5,45.8 308.8,45.8 311,45.7 313.2,45.7 315.5,45.6 317.8,45.6 320,45.6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"104\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"104\" y2=\"26\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"104\" y=\"190\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">τ</text><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"93\" x2=\"320\" y2=\"93\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"46\" y=\"97\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"></text></svg>","figure_alt":"Normalized first-order step response; a dashed vertical line marks t = tau."},{"id":"step-resp-r2-q1","round":2,"type":"numeric","prompt":"A first-order system with unit DC gain and \\(\\tau=0.8\\ \\mathrm{s}\\) starts at rest. A step of height 3 is applied at \\(t=0\\). What is the output at \\(t=1.2\\ \\mathrm{s}\\)?","answer":2.33061,"unit":"","tolerance":0.02,"explanation":"\\(y(t)=3\\left(1-e^{-t/0.8}\\right)\\). At \\(t=1.2\\): \\(t/\\tau=1.5\\), \\(e^{-1.5}=0.2231\\), so \\(y=3(0.7769)=2.33\\).\n• \\(3e^{-1.5}=0.67\\) is the remaining distance to the final value, not the output.\n• Using \\(t\\tau\\) instead of \\(t/\\tau\\) in the exponent gives about 1.85.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 210\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Step response of a first-order system rising toward 3; the time t = 1.2 s is marked.\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" style=\"max-width:340px;width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"176\"/><polygon points=\"330,176 323.6,178.7 323.6,173.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"16\"/><polygon points=\"50,16 52.7,22.4 47.3,22.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"192\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">t (s)</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"12\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">y(t)</text><polyline points=\"50,176 52.2,170.6 54.5,165.5 56.8,160.6 59,155.8 61.2,151.3 63.5,147 65.8,142.8 68,138.8 70.2,134.9 72.5,131.3 74.8,128.1 77,124.3 79.2,121.1 81.5,118 83.8,115 86,112.1 88.2,109.4 90.5,106.7 92.8,104.2 95,101.8 97.2,99.4 99.5,97.4 101.8,95 104,93 106.2,91 108.5,89.1 110.8,87.3 113,85.6 115.2,83.9 117.5,82.3 119.8,80.8 122,79.3 124.2,77.9 126.5,76.5 128.8,75.2 131,74 133.2,72.8 135.5,71.6 137.8,70.5 140,69.5 142.2,68.5 144.5,67.5 146.8,66.6 149,65.8 151.2,64.8 153.5,64 155.8,63.2 158,62.5 160.2,61.7 162.5,61 164.8,60.4 167,59.7 169.2,59.1 171.5,58.5 173.8,58 176,57.4 178.2,56.9 180.5,56.4 182.8,55.9 185,55.5 187.2,55 189.5,54.6 191.8,54.2 194,53.8 196.2,53.4 198.5,53.1 200.8,52.7 203,52.4 205.2,52.1 207.5,51.8 209.8,51.5 212,51.2 214.2,51 216.5,50.7 218.8,50.5 221,50.2 223.2,50 225.5,49.8 227.8,49.6 230,49.4 232.2,49.2 234.5,49 236.8,48.8 239,48.6 241.2,48.5 243.5,48.3 245.8,48.2 248,48.1 250.2,47.9 252.5,47.8 254.8,47.6 257,47.5 259.2,47.4 261.5,47.3 263.8,47.2 266,47.1 268.2,47 270.5,46.9 272.8,46.8 275,46.7 277.2,46.6 279.5,46.6 281.8,46.5 284,46.4 286.2,46.3 288.5,46.3 290.8,46.2 293,46.1 295.2,46.1 297.5,46 299.8,46 302,45.9 304.2,45.9 306.5,45.8 308.8,45.8 311,45.7 313.2,45.7 315.5,45.6 317.8,45.6 320,45.6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"131\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"131\" y2=\"26\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"131\" y=\"190\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">1.2 s</text></svg>","figure_alt":"Step response of a first-order system rising toward 3; the time t = 1.2 s is marked."},{"id":"step-resp-r2-q2","round":2,"type":"numeric","prompt":"A first-order system has \\(\\tau=2.5\\ \\mathrm{s}\\). After a step from rest, how long does the output take to reach 90% of its final value, in seconds?","answer":5.75646,"unit":"s","tolerance":0.02,"explanation":"Solve \\(1-e^{-t/\\tau}=0.9\\Rightarrow e^{-t/\\tau}=0.1\\Rightarrow t=\\tau\\ln10=2.303\\tau=5.76\\ \\mathrm{s}\\).\n• \\(0.9\\tau=2.25\\ \\mathrm{s}\\) assumes the rise is linear.\n• \\(\\tau\\ln0.9\\) gives a negative time because the equation was solved for the remaining fraction backwards.\n• \\(5\\tau\\) is the usual 'essentially settled' rule (more than 99%), not 90%."},{"id":"step-resp-r2-q3","round":2,"type":"mc","prompt":"An LTI system has impulse response \\(h(t)=4e^{-2t}u(t)\\) (t in seconds). What is its unit-step response?","options":["\\(s(t)=4\\left(1-e^{-2t}\\right)u(t)\\)","\\(s(t)=2\\left(1-e^{-2t}\\right)u(t)\\)","\\(s(t)=-8e^{-2t}u(t)\\)","\\(s(t)=2e^{-2t}u(t)\\)"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Integrate the impulse response: \\(\\int_0^t4e^{-2\\tau}d\\tau=\\tfrac{4}{2}\\left(1-e^{-2t}\\right)=2\\left(1-e^{-2t}\\right)\\). Check the final value: the area under h is \\(4/2=2\\), which is the DC gain.\n• Keeping the factor 4 forgets the \\(1/2\\) from integrating \\(e^{-2t}\\).\n• \\(-8e^{-2t}\\) is the derivative of h, not its integral.\n• \\(2e^{-2t}\\) decays to zero, but a step response settles at the DC gain.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 210\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Impulse response h(t) = 4 e^(-2t), starting at 4 and decaying.\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" style=\"max-width:340px;width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"176\"/><polygon points=\"330,176 323.6,178.7 323.6,173.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"16\"/><polygon points=\"50,16 52.7,22.4 47.3,22.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"192\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">t (s)</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"12\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">h(t)</text><polyline points=\"50,39.6 52.2,46.3 54.5,52.6 56.8,58.6 59,64.4 61.2,69.8 63.5,75 65.8,79.9 68,84.6 70.2,89.1 72.5,93.3 74.8,97.3 77,101.2 79.2,104.8 81.5,108.3 83.8,111.6 86,114.7 88.2,117.7 90.5,120.6 92.8,123.3 95,125.8 97.2,128.3 99.5,130.6 101.8,132.8 104,134.9 106.2,136.9 108.5,138.8 110.8,140.6 113,142.4 115.2,144 117.5,145.6 119.8,147.1 122,148.5 124.2,149.8 126.5,151.1 128.8,152.3 131,153.5 133.2,154.6 135.5,155.6 137.8,156.6 140,157.5 142.2,158.4 144.5,159.3 146.8,160.1 149,160.9 151.2,161.6 153.5,162.3 155.8,163 158,163.6 160.2,164.2 162.5,164.8 164.8,165.4 167,165.9 169.2,166.4 171.5,166.8 173.8,167.3 176,167.7 178.2,168.1 180.5,168.5 182.8,168.9 185,169.2 187.2,169.5 189.5,169.9 191.8,170.2 194,170.4 196.2,170.7 198.5,171 200.8,171.2 203,171.4 205.2,171.7 207.5,171.9 209.8,172.1 212,172.3 214.2,172.5 216.5,172.6 218.8,172.8 221,172.9 223.2,173.1 225.5,173.2 227.8,173.4 230,173.5 232.2,173.6 234.5,173.7 236.8,173.9 239,174 241.2,174.1 243.5,174.1 245.7,174.2 248,174.3 250.2,174.4 252.5,174.5 254.8,174.6 257,174.6 259.2,174.7 261.5,174.8 263.8,174.8 266,174.9 268.2,174.9 270.5,175 272.8,175 275,175.1 277.2,175.1 279.5,175.2 281.8,175.2 284,175.2 286.2,175.3 288.5,175.3 290.8,175.4 293,175.4 295.2,175.4 297.5,175.4 299.8,175.5 302,175.5 304.2,175.5 306.5,175.5 308.8,175.6 311,175.6 313.2,175.6 315.5,175.6 317.8,175.6 320,175.7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></svg>","figure_alt":"Impulse response h(t) = 4 e^(-2t), starting at 4 and decaying."},{"id":"step-resp-r3-q1","round":3,"type":"numeric","prompt":"A first-order system with unit DC gain and \\(\\tau=0.5\\ \\mathrm{s}\\) starts at rest. Its input is a pulse of height 2 from \\(t=0\\) to \\(t=1\\ \\mathrm{s}\\), then 0. What is the output at \\(t=1.5\\ \\mathrm{s}\\)?","answer":0.636185,"unit":"","tolerance":0.02,"explanation":"While the pulse is on, \\(y\\) rises toward 2: \\(y(1)=2\\left(1-e^{-2}\\right)=1.729\\). After the input turns off, y decays from that value toward 0: \\(y(1.5)=1.729\\,e^{-0.5/0.5}=1.729\\times0.368=0.636\\).\n• \\(2e^{-1}=0.74\\) assumes y had already reached 2 when the pulse ended.\n• Using \\(e^{-1.5/0.5}\\) measures the decay from \\(t=0\\) instead of from the moment the input switched off.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 210\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Input: a pulse of height 2 from t = 0 to t = 1 s, then zero.\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" style=\"max-width:340px;width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"176\"/><polygon points=\"330,176 323.6,178.7 323.6,173.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"16\"/><polygon points=\"50,16 52.7,22.4 47.3,22.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"192\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">t (s)</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"12\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">x(t)</text><polyline points=\"50,60.6 52.2,60.6 54.5,60.6 56.8,60.6 59,60.6 61.2,60.6 63.5,60.6 65.8,60.6 68,60.6 70.2,60.6 72.5,60.6 74.8,60.6 77,60.6 79.2,60.6 81.5,60.6 83.8,60.6 86,60.6 88.2,60.6 90.5,60.6 92.8,60.6 95,60.6 97.2,60.6 99.5,60.6 101.8,60.6 104,60.6 106.2,60.6 108.5,60.6 110.8,60.6 113,60.6 115.2,60.6 117.5,60.6 119.8,60.6 122,60.6 124.2,60.6 126.5,60.6 128.8,60.6 131,60.6 133.2,60.6 135.5,60.6 137.8,60.6 140,176 142.2,176 144.5,176 146.8,176 149,176 151.2,176 153.5,176 155.8,176 158,176 160.2,176 162.5,176 164.8,176 167,176 169.2,176 171.5,176 173.8,176 176,176 178.2,176 180.5,176 182.8,176 185,176 187.2,176 189.5,176 191.8,176 194,176 196.2,176 198.5,176 200.8,176 203,176 205.2,176 207.5,176 209.8,176 212,176 214.2,176 216.5,176 218.8,176 221,176 223.2,176 225.5,176 227.8,176 230,176 232.2,176 234.5,176 236.8,176 239,176 241.2,176 243.5,176 245.7,176 248,176 250.2,176 252.5,176 254.8,176 257,176 259.2,176 261.5,176 263.8,176 266,176 268.2,176 270.5,176 272.8,176 275,176 277.2,176 279.5,176 281.8,176 284,176 286.2,176 288.5,176 290.8,176 293,176 295.2,176 297.5,176 299.8,176 302,176 304.2,176 306.5,176 308.8,176 311,176 313.2,176 315.5,176 317.8,176 320,176\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></svg>","figure_alt":"Input: a pulse of height 2 from t = 0 to t = 1 s, then zero."},{"id":"step-resp-r3-q2","round":3,"type":"mc","prompt":"For \\(y(t)=y_\\infty\\left(1-e^{-t/\\tau}\\right)\\), draw the tangent to the curve at \\(t=0\\) and extend it. Where does this straight line reach the final value \\(y_\\infty\\)?","options":["At \\(t=5\\tau\\), where the response is essentially settled","Never: the tangent stays below the curve","At \\(t=\\tau\\), because the initial slope is \\(y_\\infty/\\tau\\)","At \\(t=\\tau\\ln2\\)"],"correct_index":2,"explanation":"\\(dy/dt=(y_\\infty/\\tau)e^{-t/\\tau}\\), which is \\(y_\\infty/\\tau\\) at \\(t=0\\). A line with that slope covers the full distance \\(y_\\infty\\) in exactly one time constant. This gives a quick graphical way to read \\(\\tau\\) off a measured step response.\n• \\(5\\tau\\) is where the curve itself is within 1%.\n• The tangent lies above the concave curve and crosses \\(y_\\infty\\) at a finite time.\n• \\(\\tau\\ln2\\) is the time to 50%.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 210\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Normalized step response with its dashed initial tangent line rising to the final value.\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" style=\"max-width:340px;width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"176\"/><polygon points=\"330,176 323.6,178.7 323.6,173.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"16\"/><polygon points=\"50,16 52.7,22.4 47.3,22.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"192\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">t / τ</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"12\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">y / y∞</text><polyline points=\"50,176 52.2,171.7 54.5,167.6 56.8,163.6 59,15